    },
    {
      "id": "039efc98010639306b73b2e89fe76c48a337a96dd9783b529b4db01723d71b34",
      "text": "On this page",
      "hash": "b5658fc8edda24f9c94eabac9e536e0a18e3055a8ca255f9d1b8f256ea02a6cc"
    },
    {
      "id": "4615d5298cb48e992ff6d17078934f1c7822f0bf33b3a1e1df31830a96107869",
      "text": "Why",
      "hash": "d3ae14a50bfe463f804c73c9fd16e88c36bf5a0bf4a56f98ae696a91eb2de149"
    },
    {
      "id": "c8ac174cfc93fccf6c67c76d15a5792bb441b7857ba86461d3acc137c1a8c2cc",
      "text": "Doesn't Work",
      "hash": "ef9ade7fcd79abce467972cfd4f921842867a552c5e3e07bf149cd35c7bd441b"
    },
    {
      "id": "4181050ed3b7c3ce515d357684b6b97ed64cd80f3dff51f25e8a8e84ecf86a77",
      "text": "Why Doesn't",
      "hash": "d93cf0fefa64cbdacab88849a4a34542cf290b5891f39f8c33ce9a3fb2c83475"
    },
    {
      "id": "3ce5cdb0d3e7f242ac83a3c02611067239e9fcc2d7eaf623c7294f1e6533e4ae",
      "text": "Have This Problem?",
      "hash": "29785a8d0f003c147ccd047f6574223d4ca04ed46aa9a98500cb7d1d20ab059c"
    },
    {
      "id": "4f51d99f617cc2143997f883000e293edb1c3e3ed5a787cc65bb2c62b90b280d",
      "text": "How to Log",
      "hash": "4b0b40df0ce689177427df8c0f16703c7210f66f5202670cd48dfa6f6ec83822"
    },
    {
      "id": "78e0fd01798cb669094c43211a6560e56ac883ed03ffecebd65bf2fde1156add",
      "text": "A Possible Alternative: Notifications",
      "hash": "46b4698bbd4e8bd9aca5240cdd374d1fbbfe593e4127f9908283c9a2027b5327"
    },
    {
      "id": "1466b5c05df55c5c208c549588aff744613ec37adfc2f9c7dc25a9f2aa9df44c",
      "text": "Another Possible Alternative:",
      "hash": "6624eaf6b2b45d19340477f986aadfcd855f1ebbd4e682bcc72508aa544b97e5"
    },
    {
      "id": "5afb5396de97aec6bb670a2cde7eec8ecb9807e66867f0a9e61277fd3904cb2d",
      "text": "Conclusion",
      "hash": "89db2ad881f29c18b305a20c8ed7bdffdfde49d633c27a83bd204bf9cfedaba3"
    },
    {
      "id": "00619a2eb5ead48bd7708bdd03365093d0e6ca319422546b158c6964941cabde",
      "text": "Up next",
      "hash": "e31da5b25f8b7324861e9aadaf5c503e7fd43e739fa3be17ebe63e999fb13df1"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f4405e4b8039ffaaa39cb26456f5d027b5f31df2f7a6e85d79da72fcd1fe317",
      "text": "There's a really easy foot gun that you can trigger when you're using the",
      "hash": "250bf0e149c36b3c04baf4ac65a37bf759b5dec6624983d5460b583cc8185563"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa36a6428d2552783901b5a17549f5a016945007fea0b1d437c5cabc6bb93f4b",
      "text": "transport with an MCP server.",
      "hash": "bfd6c9be9528035b47507eb59466069a6b4bfa9bd519d592c54bf2bd8b7b168a"
    },
    {
      "id": "3497c553ff844c480fbec52c3a16a29bb8f8a9e45ffaa85faca49c8eb0c1ab79",
      "text": "Here it is: console logs don't work.",
      "hash": "6176443eed4ffbdcc51a1c690305a80f47b6d92e9163c46de5a970a47d7b4276"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4a02805189b8f969e9877804aa915c1985470bbb30ccb1006655a5075f46642",
      "text": "An MCP server is really just a standard Node application. The client runs the MCP server, and monitors the",
      "hash": "0dfb6597bf04b53bad61d63764d27b997529ec6db441fbedef12cfd192b253f7"
    },
    {
      "id": "89168bf888ce70f0888be6770dc49dda9fb73e6c2f47c008a2fd29e930c84045",
      "text": "of the server for any MCP messages. It then sends back MCP messages to the server's",
      "hash": "cb119d49aa9133a67749e2b9dbef57ea6f24496ce8e0cb52766f741df21bbbd7"
    },
    {
      "id": "e60597e672aebd3e6b783b66a07ce5b4cb8b74d4b055837d3a8c12af52527bbc",
      "text": "However, Node apps use stdio for another purpose: logging. When you log to the console, you're writing to the same stream that the MCP server is using to communicate with the client.",
      "hash": "311b96b88008b9e5719ced41369fa21c783c151c121d4e89fe296f3fdb6f8644"
    },
    {
      "id": "31a02b13d4f9fd91f66746aa2ea3a957f5f174d89fd7168f5db89737f1581491",
      "text": "This means that if you log to the console in your server, you're going to be sending messages to the client that aren't MCP-formatted. Depending on the client, this could cause it to crash. And at the very least, your logs will be swallowed by the program consuming them.",
      "hash": "d6ac0f03713926dc94c93ee8365d33be82a96ee3062f5141940a4baefabdd0f7"
    },
    {
      "id": "cad034969df1b78df1249f10f8f7e323036acadab54eac1d12ca0a20daacbe2b",
      "text": "Go deeper:",
      "hash": "15ad3d88c6733d9b257c322d3afecc9bce2b18558171007db87598c118ca17f9"
    },
    {
      "id": "cc5aa03466ac6e86fe8b5558e4110370a06578cc75b5877678ccd066953dd12f",
      "text": "join the waitlist for AI Coding for Real Engineers",
      "hash": "16c3492a8464a0859c944e287a9d433e9a2635f22a6bd8aad59f88c3e80ab732"
    },
    {
      "id": "f41dc5dd7b02e11fb00f1e16475fa148a3a572091bea0e54725551f1caf535e5",
      "text": "The",
      "hash": "b344d80e24a3679999fa964450b34bc24d1578a35509f934c1418b0a20d21a67"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c2ff671a792c035b0b5166035a5ac8a7aa727ab7756516d1dafa6ff9a976122",
      "text": "transport doesn't have this problem because it doesn't use",
      "hash": "972c6c4e45cc013cac0efb6aed0cbdef85fe4cb0f2848dc77734f33f5a41547f"
    },
    {
      "id": "ade61ac21a11819187ac2683d3fb48ff87574f68ae04fd22a0e34f4f92c988b6",
      "text": "for transporting messages:",
      "hash": "d07f64f648947baffa3524385a54863432be997ae0a7255c0ec83919619611d7"
    },
    {
      "id": "d3ae4c8e0908bd4b6c1e50e7e5de2dd713cfaed8e0fce89d419c6f1266b0ee38",
      "text": "This means that it's free to use",
      "hash": "2ab66adf2e53d5300f9c33e5b0b391532d94ea35c3f0ac3e3302155046fabb50"
    },
    {
      "id": "c78272d97bf7b8b19e2353867c9fe4763811d909a5ea6726e977cd074e002157",
      "text": "for logging.",
      "hash": "51f4611a3144a5190c5f914cac8aa299a2f759c095aa2f782882b03bd8d8070e"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ada0af130362263bf6c49393b34e7164219ed7dd42735decbb860f0148f4137",
      "text": "It's perfectly possible to use",
      "hash": "d2706fd9cd22ed867be0991241a2aeba6d3639614e85e03725bc77a2679cb651"
    },
    {
      "id": "61487c4619737967807800b5eb22afcaaee18598e965a31012c6bb997ab37bfa",
      "text": "locally, so you may prefer using that method if accessing the console is important to you.",
      "hash": "fd280d748594d86cd2be30bea7b638253377cd09b6b9870b417b8c0f92fc48ec"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef88924a632a3178be2dce815d04e3fc2c109cfc821bc29b6def94a23b8e8d98",
      "text": "My preferred solution is to create a custom logger that writes to a local file -",
      "hash": "3c73787aefb157df5f6190ceb1199d1587663222c1bf9741fdd1550d0c55803d"
    },
    {
      "id": "1f9f19e446aeff85d44e6c0e491668ed0e7e521a2a70ef6095e7699f44da5fcc",
      "text": ". Here's my implementation:",
      "hash": "3050e83ddf5acf34b6c14c8ca3a5de59dedabc1e2462a543aa600460c11e2f63"
    },
    {
      "id": "5995cb4fd40c94bf9341e3a20e58cde6d38603733715b316d6d0a4e2b721ffa2",
      "text": "We use",
      "hash": "f07f38e48a196903e189132b1c870b6a9313913c3cc9cb57608cb259c66e75e3"
    },
    {
      "id": "f3288b41edd7ab0f09ca64b8a540ff4f6df95045a6ac5a798152661ea52127d0",
      "text": "to write to a file synchronously.",
      "hash": "24e8297033318e9ff5ff0572a1af2e11df188355d2e64be89b6ad8fe798b8afc"
    },
    {
      "id": "53d984c61b42157e6e220f5abf5f47ac1556708a098ff524b1388cd95026d222",
      "text": "We define the path to the log file.",
      "hash": "366fbad9ee2bb616f1ddb6169c7c07b20027b7bc24dd66de7ae44971d7117b59"
    },
    {
      "id": "ca87bf75dfaaf0be178234f8e20f9ffcbae37e2ae0ec5af3fb790875a57ef9a3",
      "text": "We define a function to format the message.",
      "hash": "4d8088b394e971058b16354e39742c8dde223eb7d2c5258a149d70d6dc34cd8e"
    },
    {
      "id": "5517d170a6bc98bcaf21567932995f4f99c515d8a24eae9086343c517763ac14",
      "text": "We export a logger object with a",
      "hash": "7b98180e7552d05fa1177dd99092c48ec3089ce200ca14211fb031b741b28465"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f0fb1325c4c4e68f6bce31a7d1caaa2f42fa055c20fa7b19be14653bce9c558",
      "text": "method that writes to the log file. You can export other methods like",
      "hash": "7f7eb6e5e1644698b60bb6e265948bf9856c97afae120a5223cd7aaf22be971e"
    },
    {
      "id": "cada8deb2afa9dfde84583b66984c3fbcaccd60faf2a5dc50e8589c03f62a5c4",
      "text": ", etc.",
      "hash": "3a1706477c8f9bb84217bd3efeb1eebc69db5246c08b2764c01b087260a2e139"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab0ebffac43f561c36b2b6857c5b4abc34adeee273089d58d928fd5d290cb054",
      "text": "This way, you can log to a file without interfering with the MCP protocol.",
      "hash": "b99a05ac46ee20d9951aa5360839788a371ba9a995c70bc85aaeee65bc7ea276"
    },
    {
      "id": "31d28ed0722fae6bb66bc9da095633d65594e7f343683e297569cf1e037673fb",
      "text": "A reader alerted me to the fact that MCP does have a concept of 'notifications', albeit somewhat buried in the",
      "hash": "c2965a7935df43fe4bfb3173c15494275895aaba29eab785938cb89a796020e7"
    },
    {
      "id": "2dfd5465df709f959d6d7ac8b58126b9f4d4bdd18f0e5cbb3511c5bff38b2adc",
      "text": "In theory, this would allow the server to send a message to the client.",
      "hash": "2495e25ba1ae4e6993a377bb1039a846cdd6fcea2480b731781fa9a0e4cc72ab"
    },
    {
      "id": "a29a111e7e76520af3e4fc0a8acbb40fdcb5052632f2ec89750821b2c10e0cfd",
      "text": "However, the implementation of this would be up to the client - so whether you could use this mechanism for logging is an open question.",
      "hash": "26dad5fd8c480c2d07562e7d8259676288072d4470678c07e884260a6637795c"
    },
    {
      "id": "ea24c5f6c081bbc28083ef46d3b950b1d0c5be694816ebc6ddf4fa3415157bcc",
      "text": "If anyone has use notifications for logging, I'd love to hear about it in the",
      "hash": "d91178fd3abf6b0b2951d542165d43eabc3e2a7e4b513245986521394c4ad8b7"
    },
    {
      "id": "45f5638a47c31a82b2bd4cea2df48f8777328a6c1ca740a7823d26f08f023550",
      "text": "Discord",
      "hash": "053bc65874ad6098e58c41c57b378a2f36b0220e5e0b46722245e6c2f796818c"
    },
    {
      "id": "d5ac68a749ae2a6af11c24fe00ac69c591ba573bc4ab29ec9aeff53c8fc4a9ba",
      "text": "I've had a tip that logging to",
      "hash": "91c85b471c419b6e3d00d25e6cf5bda8c25b6838d81153d9925c7cce47930f3c"
    },
    {
      "id": "f580310688d880aa3297e03f68abb8abcb7b09c7c3fe781369ccc726abc24f63",
      "text": "- i.e, using",
      "hash": "f762d95743ca1a8662d8cb375892ad7f51f3e13f5de76ba700eafedcb1d5a4a7"
    },
    {
      "id": "33aa6614eeef17fe18b9218bc59dce8032617aab982e3a27b0df9cfa474a1e19",
      "text": "- is not read by the MCP client.",
      "hash": "2de6e16f697206107fe5005eb8d396541dc3842f39ce5b3485d6e748685e37a2"
    },
    {
      "id": "6c3480e7246f8d9fbd54ee936d48f1318fe157277e82712644fbeb3a6fcdde7b",
      "text": "This means that you can potentially",
      "hash": "c9bc6c0ed5d8c1da2a40d82c997c76736b6b33d6110d1ccbbdd3d1d9e9183243"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1aac45c247e4c954e489166de3680e5b3b9dd05d563e296344ab5ba1010b7a6",
      "text": "the process running the MCP server, and log it out to a file.",
      "hash": "395d351bc0a4b0e076911ececf2476317dfc4d2aa2e976d6f8930a08c37481e9"
    },
    {
      "id": "6b2a2bda1ef2ec136744d7df200a66d3893ce23b3e7b90ae91f2da651b405d1d",
      "text": "I'll cover this in more depth soon - consider this a TODO.",
      "hash": "cf8b717283e09898f70d582e1d20440498dd1916f8d082dedc05b13365527c2c"
    },
    {
      "id": "4260cd452ce8958efc6c8ed98e995ec661c06858741f914072196405d360bc93",
      "text": "You've got two choices when you're considering logging in an MCP server:",
      "hash": "f6f656baff051a78ce6345439279f5e7d4b36c9187ded4709db391f2c7df45de"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a21e176d13c3ec72b0e7cf45c47f941b3ece4adabc9e40bcddd657e362092b9",
      "text": "Use a transport that doesn't interfere with",
      "hash": "8a37ffc1b2e969a2e93385c58b7eebf058e11bbdf20821b36a0124ec24d385dc"
    },
    {
      "id": "58e41b6ce2de4521bb36fa9eddd4e78f20c0698ebba71be7ad8ef83d43e9399d",
      "text": ", like",
      "hash": "14a3034a5af42f5bf56c98d1daaf7e6234fc82c1a4d13bcc8833b0f2d4c09f8e"
    },
    {
      "id": "881721cf8e243a45b4bfd2a36e2b7ded050477cf5ee86880ee85e40d320d5564",
      "text": "Write to a",
      "hash": "d524e2091b1d79e9339a7022f0f319226f9591d7778d3851c40c06136efcfb8e"
    },
    {
      "id": "7bc89e680cb4cac892b4fa8783dfe09ab2ba48eb9fd38fbd659c5f6d9046fffd",
      "text": "file.",
      "hash": "eb36be6c06717c3b88700bdc0678576b33b6b4ef76de644a43b56023e9e77cb0"
    },
    {
